# v1.9.16.0, a Tool-Mapping Line Above an Inlined Persona

The agent personas name Claude Code tools, and `codex exec` has only its shell. A read-only dispatch that inlined the `context` persona once read nothing and still exited 0. Rule 17 now requires a line that tells the child which shell commands stand in for the persona's tools.

> Spec folder: `specs/agents/006-agent-contract-and-registry-alignment/006-codex-persona-tool-mapping`

&nbsp;

## What's New at a Glance

- **Rule 17 requires a tool-mapping line above the inlined persona.** The rule holds the literal text to copy. It names read commands only: `cat`, `sed -n`, `rg`, `find`, `ls` and `wc`.
- **A sixth dispatch gotcha names the failure.** A read-only run can exit 0 with a report that ends `FILES READ: none`. Ask for a `FILES READ:` line and treat an empty one as a failed dispatch.
- **The failure is intermittent.** It was observed on codex-cli 0.167.2. On codex-cli 0.169.0 the same prompt read its file with the line and without it.
- **The canonical persona contract states the rule for every CLI.** `sk-prompt/assets/cli-prompt-quality-card.md` section 6.3 requires the line wherever the child's tools differ from the persona's.
